---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { RETENTION_DAYS, RATE } from '../../functions/_lib/rules';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="What this site stores, who can see it, how long it's kept and how to have it removed."
>
  <article class="wrap--narrow section prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Short version: no trackers, no analytics, no ads and no visitor cookies. If you send feedback,
      it's stored so Travis can read it. It's only shown publicly if you chose public and it was
      approved.
    </p>
    <p class="hint">
      Last updated 23 October 2026. This page describes how the site actually works. It isn't a
      claim of compliance with any particular law.
    </p>

    <h2>Browsing</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        No analytics, tracking pixels, advertising, social embeds or third-party fonts. Fonts and
        images are served from this site.
      </li>
      <li>
        No cookies are set for visitors. The only cookie is the owner's sign-in cookie for
        moderation.
      </li>
      <li>
        Two optional preferences are kept in your own browser's storage and never sent anywhere:
        low-glow reading mode, and the ticks on a project's setup trail. Clear your site data to
        remove them.
      </li>
      <li>
        Like any website, the hosting provider (Cloudflare) processes your IP address and request
        details to deliver pages and protect against abuse.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Downloads</h2>
    <p>
      Download buttons link directly to the apps' public GitHub releases, so the file comes from
      GitHub (github.com and its download servers), and GitHub's own privacy statement applies to
      that request. QR codes on this site are generated when the site is built, so no link is ever
      sent to a QR service.
    </p>

    <h2>Feedback</h2>
    <h3>What's stored</h3>
    <p>
      The type, the project it's about, public or private, your title and message, an optional
      display name, an optional reply email, any bug-report details you fill in, and the date. It's
      stored in a database on the site's hosting provider.
    </p>
    <h3>Who can see it</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Public feedback</strong> starts as pending. Only after Travis approves it are the
        type, project, title, message, display name (or "Anonymous"), date and any public reply
        shown on the site.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Private reports</strong> are only ever visible to Travis. The system refuses to
        publish them.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Reply emails</strong> are only visible to Travis, only used to reply to you, and
        never shown publicly.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Abuse protection</h3>
    <p>
      To limit spam, the server keeps a salted, one-way hash of your IP address for up to 24 hours
      to count submissions (at most {RATE.submitPer10Min} per 10 minutes and {RATE.submitPerDay} per
      day). Your IP address isn't stored with your feedback. Identical messages sent within a day
      are refused as duplicates.
    </p>
    <h3>How long it's kept</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Rejected or spam submissions: the content is erased {RETENTION_DAYS.rejected} days after the
        decision.
      </li>
      <li>Removed submissions: the content is erased immediately.</li>
      <li>
        Reply emails: erased {RETENTION_DAYS.email} days after you submit, whatever the status.
      </li>
      <li>
        Approved public feedback: kept until you ask for it to be removed, or it's removed under the
        community guidelines.
      </li>
      <li>
        Pending items and private reports: kept until Travis handles them. There's no fixed limit.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Erasing keeps a minimal record that an item existed, with its date, type, project and status,
      plus an owner-only log of moderation actions (which action and when, with no content). If the
      owner makes a database backup, erased content may remain in that backup until it's replaced.
    </p>

    <h3>Removal requests</h3>
    <p>
      Send a private report through the <a href="/feedback">feedback form</a> with the reference
      shown on your receipt, or enough detail to find the item. It will be removed and its content
      erased.
    </p>

    <h2>Please don't send</h2>
    <p>
      Passwords, API or licence keys, unredacted logs, VINs, or other vehicle and device
      identifiers. File uploads aren't accepted.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
